  "question": {
    "text": "A child of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is going round a merry-go-round that makes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> rotation in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The radius of the merry-go-round is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The centrifugal force on the child will be",
    "image": null
